1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Harlan Sanders, better known as Colonel Sanders, is the founder of KFC, Kentucky Fried Chicken.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
But success didn't come easily for him. It came very, very late. At age 5, his father died.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
At age 16, he dropped out of school. At age 17, he lost four different jobs.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:26,000
At age 18, he got married. By age 20, he had a baby and separated from his wife.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Throughout his life, he worked many jobs. Farmhand, streetcar conductor, railroad worker,

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
insurance salesman, and even ran a ferryboat company. But he failed at almost everything.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
In his 40s, he started cooking for travelers at a gas station he owned. He didn't have a

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:51,000
restaurant. He served people on his own dining table. Over time, he perfected his secret recipe

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:58,000
of fried chicken, a recipe of 11 herbs and spices. But when he tried to franchise his

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,000
chicken recipe at age 65, he was rejected over 1,000 times. That's not a typo. 1,000 times.

11
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Imagine being 65 years old, broke, living off a tiny $105 Social Security check,

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,000
and still believing you can succeed. But he didn't give up. Finally, someone gave him a chance,

13
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:27,000
and from there, KFC was born. Today, KFC is one of the largest fast food chains in the world,

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:35,000
with thousands of outlets across the globe.

